# Citing [= project_name =]

[% if paper %]
If [= project_name =] helps your work, please cite its paper:

> [% for author in paper.authors %][= author.family =] [= author.given[0] =][% if not loop.last %], [% endif %][% endfor %].
> [= paper.title =]. *[= paper.journal =]* ([= paper.year =]).
> [doi:[= paper.doi =]](https://doi.org/[= paper.doi =])

[% endif %]
[% if doi %]
To cite the software itself, [= project_name =]'s versions are archived on
Zenodo: [doi:[= doi =]](https://doi.org/[= doi =]) names them all, and each
version has a DOI of its own there.
[% else %]
To cite the software itself, name its version (`[= command =] --version`) and
its repository, <https://github.com/[= owner =]/[= repository =]>.
[% endif %]

GitHub's *Cite this repository* button gives the citation in APA and BibTeX,
from `CITATION.cff`.
